# Simfinity Development Guidelines

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode, functional components with hooks
- Next.js 15 App Router conventions, `"use client"` only when required
- Material-UI components consistently, responsive design (mobile-first)
- Import custom components via barrel: `import { X } from '@/components/custom'`
- Import registration APIs from `@simtlix/simfinity-fe-components`

## Custom Components (src/components/custom/)

Two types:
- **Form input**: props `{ value: T; onChange: (v: T) => void; disabled: boolean; error?: string }`
- **Column display**: props `{ value: string | number | null | undefined }`

Every component must have:
1. Exported props interface (`<Name>Props`)
2. Storybook story (`<Name>.stories.tsx`) with `title: 'Custom/<Name>'`, `tags: ['autodocs']`
3. Barrel export in `index.ts` (component + type)

## When Adding a New Entity

1. Create folder `src/simfinitySetup/<entity>/`
2. Add form customization files per mode (`.create.ts`, `.edit.ts`, `.view.tsx`)
3. Add column renderers if needed (`<entity>.column.<field>.tsx`)
4. Add state machine if needed (`<entity>.stateMachine.ts`)
5. Create `index.ts` that wires all registrations
6. Import and call from `src/simfinitySetup/index.ts`
7. Add i18n labels to `public/i18n/en.json`, `public/i18n/es.json`
8. Add function labels to `src/simfinitySetup/i18n/i18n.setup.ts` if needed

## When Adding a Custom Component

1. Create `src/components/custom/<Name>.tsx` with typed props interface
2. Create `src/components/custom/<Name>.stories.tsx`
3. Add exports to `src/components/custom/index.ts`
4. Verify with `npm run storybook`

## When Modifying Form Customizations

- Use the correct mode (create/edit/view) — they are independent
- Stepper forms require `mode: "stepper"` + `steps[]` + `stepId` on each field
- Custom renderers using JSX require `.tsx` extension
- Always wire new registration functions in the entity's `index.ts`
